# Oros lore lock

The curated lorebook in `docs/lore/` (chapters I–X) and the Appendix in `docs/terminology.md` are the leading truth for **Brightcall**. Start from `docs/lore/README.md`.

## Before any lore or GDD change

1. **Conflict check first (mandatory).** Compare the request to `docs/terminology.md`, `docs/lore/` chapters, and this rule. If anything **conflicts**, **disagrees**, or would **rename / retire / reverse** a locked fact: **stop**. Do **not** edit yet. List each conflict in chat (old lock → proposed change → why it matters) and wait for Dirk's call. A "master blueprint," paste, or full rewrite does **not** skip this step.
2. Only after conflicts are resolved (or Dirk says overwrite) may you edit. Compatible additions and non-conflicting expansions may proceed.
3. **Full-doc consistency pass (mandatory after any approved lore change).** Before commit, search and align **all** of: `docs/terminology.md`, `docs/lore/**` chapters, `docs/factions/**`, `docs/gdd/**`, `docs/README.md`, `site/src/content/**`, related site pages, and `.cursor/rules/aethora-lore-lock.mdc`. No leftover retired names, no one-file-only updates, no half-applied locks.
4. Write **English only** in all docs, even if the user prompt is in another language.
5. **Overwrite** outdated paragraphs once a change is approved. Do not annotate corrections. Do not keep "formerly called X" or "do not call it Y" in narrative.
6. Affirmative prose only: state what the world **is**.
7. Forget retired names in story text. Legacy words live only in terminology's retired list.

## Locked pillars (summary)

- Game: **Brightcall** (one word)
- Genre: **Bright-punk** — between fantasy and sci-fi; modern-gloomy steampunk cousin; extreme high contrast; Sin City read (Bone/Ash/Greige dominant + **sparse** Magenta/Cyan/Gold Chroma hazard accents). Chroma is rareish and dangerous — not wall paint. Master plate: `site/public/art/hero-harvester.png`
- Hard tech limit: **no** computers, screens, LEDs, internet, or modern firearms; Bright energy (bright white) or Chroma (volatile neon)
- **Brilliance:** rare cast-to-fit; **Kardia/Vesper body budget:** one full arm + shoulder + one glove on the other hand
- World: **Oros** · Anomaly: **The Bright** (vast **cube**); **Seeds** = spawning zones; end → must rise elsewhere (faith: one reincarnated; science: many instances, one law); Resting Light cities at Seed intersections
- **Interior:** peristaltic brutalist maze guiding organics to Core; **fractured gravity** + parkour mobility; torn Kardia/Aureate structures as poor reality reflections; civic cloth-first kit (no sealed exosuits / hazard-suit mechs)
- **Bright Core:** blinding white **sphere** of liquid light (reverse black hole); Core *interior* unknown; cube = Eclipse shell only
- **Call / calling / Brightcall:** one multilayered pull; physical read = maze + gravity toward Core; sensory form still open
- **Eclipse / Umbra / Exit:** Null-Flint harvest or destroy only → Stitching
- **Seams / Enhancement / Bloom / Splinter-Crush:** burst + continuous weep; wraps; Bloom internal-only; Enhancement tiers (Weak/Moderate/Ultimate) are **table language only**, not lore nouns — enhancements vary a lot in the world; Seam violence escalates with organics / combat stress
- **Peoples:** **Humans** most common city race; **Oru** rare indigenous exception (Vesper). Valen is human
- **Bright cells:** Eminence-pattern (VE-3) **cubes** (~7.5 cm); bright-white charge (cyan is Chroma); swap charged / discard empty; Harvester Tithe often 2–3 per run; white steam vent. Vesper: issued cells + empty legacy smith-era cell
- **Resonance:** craft family; Glaive-class forged in **Bright Core–powered smithy**; weapon runs on Bright cells. Vesper trenchcoat is **unique to her** (not Kardia uniform). Valen: muscular human + slender Chroma arm + Resonance-inspired Chroma dagger (name TBD) — fundamentally different drive (Chroma, no Bright cell)
- Quantum / lab Seam model: **still in progress** — do not lock
- **House Kardia:** large former Bright-order superpower; Brightsmith craft remains; Core-powered smithies; Aureate took control; civic fashion varies — trench is Vesper’s
- **Aureate:** former Kardia; barons/crime lords; syndicate methods; Chroma-fuel; **controlled-Bloom infantry**; heavier metal; Chroma exhaust ~60% Magenta / 35% Cyan / 15% Gold; **Valen** = exiled human Chroma-Smith (slender prosthesis + sneaky Resonance-inspired dagger); Kardia Chroma stigma
- **Refract Labs:** Splinter-Crush weaponizers
- **Lumari:** divine spiritualists; excess Bloom; Seam-crack teleport **open** (not locked)
- **Penumbra:** Bright unnatural; look down on dependence; **leverage Bloomed cells/bodies** (method open) — no "Voice"
- **the Oru:** Indigenous Wardens (faction); Null-Flint; anti-harvest; natural harmony; opposite of Penumbra. Race **Oru** is broader — city Oru exist; Vesper is Oru in Kardia and stands out; Harvester work conflicts with warden ideology without requiring the word traitor
- Eras: First Light → Traveling Light → Resting Light
- Match mutation: Splintered · No Weld
- Retired: Brightforged; **Aethora** (world is **Oros**); **Kho'Lan** (faction is **the Oru**); Adumbra; Vertex/Axiom Labs; Altered Humans; cyan Bright-cell charge; locked third-quantum-field model; The Voice; the Syndicate as faction name; sealed exosuits / hazard-suit mechs as Harvester identity; Husks / The Lost as locked NPC class

